.SS GET_MFSPR_287
.IP
.EX
#define GET_MFSPR_287(VARIABLE)
#define get_mfspr_287(variable)
.EE
.PP
Executes the \f[CR]mfspr\f[R] instruction targeting \f[B]SPR 287\f[R],
storing the retrieved value into the provided variable.
.PP
The macro emits an \f[CR]mfspr\f[R] instruction where:
.IP \(bu 2
The destination is a general\-purpose register mapped to the given
variable
.IP \(bu 2
The source is \f[B]SPR 287\f[R]
.PP
After execution, the variable contains the raw 32\-bit or 64\-bit value
of the register (depending on the processor mode).
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
unsigned int value;

get_mfspr_287(value);
.EE
.PP
After execution:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]value\f[R] contains the contents of \f[B]SPR 287\f[R]
